#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
iv-suggest - lane based suggestion playlists for Invidious (LXC 109).

A lane is one server side playlist plus the rules that fill it. Adding a genre
is a new block in the config file, not new code.

Several accounts share one instance: lanes.yml holds the library of lanes and a
users: block saying who gets which, and the bot issues itself one Invidious
session per account rather than holding a token for each. An account not named
in that block is never touched.

  config : /etc/iv-suggest/lanes.yml and /etc/iv-suggest/env (docs/CONFIG.md)
  auth   : one session per account, in suggest.accounts, minted on demand
  state  : PostgreSQL schema "suggest" in the Invidious database
  usage  : iv-suggest --help

Rate limiting: every call to /api/v1/videos/<id> makes Invidious fetch from
YouTube, because the Invidious video cache is UNLOGGED and short lived. The
bot therefore keeps its own permanent metadata cache, paces the remaining
calls, and stops at a hard budget per run.
"""

